ion` initially reported \"Script not found `tests/integration`\". This is because the npm script runs `bun tests/integration` (treating it as a script file), but the correct invocation is `bun test tests/integration`. This is a pre-existing quirk, not a regression.\n\n### Step 6.2: Schema generation\n\n- `bun run generate-schemas`: **PASS**. Schemas written to both `schemas/` (runtime) and `docs/public/schemas/` (docs site) as expected.\n- All three schemas generated: `hank.schema.json`, `hankweave.schema.json`, `sentinel.schema.json`.\n\n### Step 6.3: Runtime build\n\n- `bun run build`: **PASS**. `dist/index.js` created (1799.54 KB, minified). Build completes cleanly.\n\n### Step 6.4: Docs build\n\n- `bun run --cwd docs build`: **PASS**. Next.js build succeeds across all routes. The `postbuild` pagefind step (`pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind`) runs and indexes 32 pages (5,377 words).\n\n### Step 6.5: npm pack\n\n- `npm pack --dry-run`: **PASS**. Tarball contains only `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`, and metadata. `docs/` is **absent** from the tarball, confirming the `\"files\"` allowlist works correctly.\n\n### Step 6.6: test-sync-local dry run\n\n- `bun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version 0.5.6 --use-head`: **Partially verified**. The test ran through Steps 1–5 (copy, clone, changelog, snapshot, sync) successfully. It stopped at Step 6 (create-tag) because tag `v0.5.6` already exists on the remote public repo. This is expected behavior, not a migration regression.\n- Manual inspection of `/tmp/hankweave-sync-test/public/` confirmed that `docs/` is **absent** from the snapshot.\n- Manual inspection of `/tmp/hankweave-sync-test/public/package.json` confirmed that `\"workspaces\"` is **absent** (correctly stripped). Name is `\"hankweave\"`, homepage points to `hankweave-runtime`.\n\n### Step 6.7: Release dry-run\n\n- `bun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks`: Correctly stopped at \"Checking working directory...\" because there are uncommitted changes (the migration itself hasn't been committed yet). This is expected behavior — the release script correctly requires a clean working tree. Validation logic for `docs/` in `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` could not be exercised in this state, but the code change was verified by code review (correct use of `startsWith()` matching).\n\n---\n\n## Issues Discovered During Implementation\n\n### Issue 1: `bun run test:integration` script path mismatch\n\nThe npm script `test:integration` runs `bun tests/integration`, which Bun interprets as running a script file named `tests/integration` (not a directory). The correct invocation for running a test directory is `bun test tests/integration`. The script appears to work in some contexts (perhaps when bun resolves the directory) but reported \"Script not found\" in this environment.\n\n**Severity:** Minor — does not affect the migration itself. Pre-existing quirk.\n**Impact on plan:** None. The plan's Phase 6 Step 6.1 includes `bun run test:integration`, which may behave unexpectedly depending on Bun version. Add a note that `bun test tests/integration` is the reliable invocation.\n\n### Issue 2: test-sync-local verification not reached when tag already exists\n\nThe verification section (shouldNotExist checks) comes after the create-tag step in `test-sync-local.ts`. When running against a version that already has a tag on the public remote, the test halts before verification. This means the full verification coverage (including confirming `docs` is in `shouldNotExist`) can only be confirmed on a fresh version number.\n\n**Severity:** Minor — the verification code exists and was reviewed to be correct. The issue is only with running it end-to-end during testing.\n**Impact on plan:** The plan's Step 6.6 instruction assumes verification will complete. Add a note that if running against a version that already has a public tag, use a different version number (e.g., `--version 999.0.0` with an empty public repo) or manually inspect the `/tmp/` snapshot.\n\n### Issue 3: docs/node_modules present in docs/ directory\n\nThe `docs/` directory has a `node_modules/` subdirectory (from `bun install` after workspace was configured). This is expected and correct. But when inspecting `ls docs/`, it appears alongside the source files, which may be surprising to reviewers. The `node_modules/` in `docs/` is symlinks to the hoisted root `node_modules/` (standard Bun workspace behavior).\n\n**Severity:** Informational — not a problem.\n**Impact on plan:** None. Plan correctly describes hoisting behavior.\n\n### Issue 4: docs/public/schemas/ created on first schema generation run\n\n`docs/public/schemas/` did not exist before `bun run generate-schemas` was first run. The `generate-schemas.ts` script correctly creates it via `mkdirSync({ recursive: true })`. However, this means on a fresh checkout of the migration branch (before running `generate-schemas`), `docs/public/schemas/` will be absent. The plan's optional monorepo smoke test was updated to check `docs/public/` rather than `docs/public/schemas/` for exactly this reason.\n\n**Severity:** Informational — the script handles this correctly.\n**Impact on plan:** The plan documents this correctly in Section g (\"New tests needed\"). No action needed.\n\n### Issue 5: `docs/public/_pagefind/` generated by docs build\n\nAfter `bun run --cwd docs build`, the `docs/public/_pagefind/` directory is created with the Pagefind search index. This directory is correctly gitignored (added in Phase 4). No issues.\n\n**Severity:** Informational.\n**Impact on plan:** None.\n\n---\n\n## Correctness Verification Summary\n\n| Plan Item | Status | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|-------|\n| `docs/` directory created from `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` | ✅ Correct | Flattened, no `nextra-site/` wrapper |\n| `docs/bun.lock` removed | ✅ Correct | Absent |\n| `package.json` has `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` | ✅ Correct | Placed between `\"engines\"` and `\"scripts\"` |\n| `tsconfig.json` excludes `docs/**/*` | ✅ Correct | |\n| `generate-schemas.ts` path updated | ✅ Correct | Uses `../docs/public/schemas` |\n| `sync-public.ts` STRIP_DIRS has `\"docs\"` | ✅ Correct | Bare name, no trailing slash |\n| `sync-public.ts` transformPackageJson strips workspaces | ✅ Correct | `delete pkg.workspaces` added |\n| `release.ts` INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP has `\"docs/\"` | ✅ Correct | Trailing slash, matches startsWith pattern |\n| `release.ts` schema diff check covers docs | ✅ Correct | Both dirs in `git diff --name-only` |\n| `release.ts` schema revert covers docs | ✅ Correct | `allowFailure: true` retained |\n| `release.ts` git add covers docs/public/schemas/ | ✅ Correct | |\n| `test-sync-local.ts` rsync excludes docs | ✅ Correct | `--exclude='docs'` added |\n| `test-sync-local.ts` shouldNotExist has \"docs\" | ✅ Correct | Bare name, no trailing slash |\n| `.gitignore` updated for docs build artifacts | ✅ Correct | `_pagefind/` and scoped `.next/`, `out/` |\n| `standard-operating-procedures.md` updated | ✅ Correct | All 4 subsections updated |\n| `vercel.json` carried over with CVE flag | ✅ Present | `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag retained |\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations for Plan Update\n\n1. **Phase 6 Step 6.1** — Clarify that `bun run test:integration` may behave differently from `bun test tests/integration` depending on Bun version. The direct invocation `bun test tests/integration` is more reliable.\n\n2. **Phase 6 Step 6.6** — Add a note that if the tag already exists on the remote, the test will halt before the verification section. Suggest using an alternative approach: inspect the `/tmp/hankweave-sync-test/public/` snapshot directory manually to confirm `docs/` absence and `package.json` field stripping.\n\n3. **Section g (\"Pre-existing test/check failures\")** — The `test:integration` script issue is a minor pre-existing quirk worth mentioning alongside the other pre-existing issues so future implementers don't confuse it for a regression.\n\n4. The plan is otherwise accurate and complete. The implementation matched the plan's described changes with high fidelity. No deviations or unexpected issues were found that would require structural plan changes.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:47:05.054Z"}
